 One side of a triangle is 1 and the other two are two side lengths.  Let's fix the side of length 1 and without loss of generality assume that the circle has radius 1, so the two numbers on the circle are the two <b> opposite</b> sides, and the third side is the given side of length 1.

[asy]
unitsize(1.6 cm);

