A triangle with a side length of 1 or longer is not obtuse.  A triangle is obtuse if and only if the square of its 1 longest side is greater than the sum of the squares of the 2 smaller sides.  In other words, we want the area of the sector subtended by the angle opposite our side of length 1 to be less than $\frac{1}{2}\pi - \cos^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{2}\right) = \frac{23}{24}\pi$.

